        "chapterId": 56,
        "headingId": 229,
        "headingText": "<p>9251/1 Giant cell tumour of soft parts</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-09-16T11:07:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 397,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 230,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58747,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 56,
        "headingId": 230,
        "headingText": "<p>2F7C &amp; XH81M1 Neoplasms of uncertain behaviour of connective or other soft tissue &amp; Giant cell tumour of soft parts NOS</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-01-23T16:31:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 398,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 231,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58748,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 56,
        "headingId": 231,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> giant cell tumour of low malignant potential.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:47:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 399,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 232,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58749,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 56,
        "headingId": 232,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:47:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 400,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 233,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58750,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 56,
        "headingId": 233,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Giant cell tumour of soft tissue usually occurs in superficial soft tissues of the upper and lower extremities (70% of tumours). Affected less frequently are the trunk (20%) and head and neck (7%) regions {10496598; 10716152; 10680893; 19615796; 21563092}. Occasional cases have been reported in other anatomical locations {21139924; 23644334; 29867073}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:47:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 401,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 234,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58751,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 56,
        "headingId": 234,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours usually present as painless growing masses {10716152; 10680893}, with an average duration of 6&nbsp;months {10680893}. Peripheral mineralization is common.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:47:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 402,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 235,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58752,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 56,
        "headingId": 235,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Giant cell tumour of soft tissue occurs predominantly in the fifth decade of life, but it can affect patients ranging in age from 5&nbsp;to 89&nbsp;years. Giant cell tumour of soft tissue shows no apparent difference in incidence with regard to sex or ethnicity {10496598; 10716152; 10680893}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:47:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 403,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 236,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58753,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 56,
        "headingId": 236,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:47:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 404,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 237,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58754,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 56,
        "headingId": 237,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Giant cell tumour of soft tissue lacks the mutations of the <em>H3-3A</em> (<em>H3F3A</em>) gene that are present in the vast majority of giant cell tumours of bone, suggesting a different pathogenesis {28084336; 28477388}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:47:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 411,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 244,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58755,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 56,
        "headingId": 244,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours range in size from 0.7 to 10&nbsp;cm (mean: 3&nbsp;cm) {10496598; 10716152; 10680893}. Subcutaneous adipose tissue or dermis is involved in 70% of tumours; 30% are situated deep to superficial fascia. Giant cell tumour of soft tissue is a well-circumscribed, mostly solid, nodular mass with a fleshy, reddish-brown or grey cut surface. Gritty regions of mineralized bone are frequently present at the periphery {10716152}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:47:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 405,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 238,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58756,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 56,
        "headingId": 238,
        "headingText": "<p>Giant cell tumour of soft tissue displays a multinodular architecture (85%). Cellular nodules are separated by fibrous septa of varying thickness, containing haemosiderin-laden macrophages {10716152}. The nodules are composed of a mixture of round to oval mononuclear cells and osteoclast-like multinucleated giant cells, with both cell types immersed in a richly vascularized stroma. Mitotic activity is readily seen in giant cell tumour of soft tissue {10496598; 10716152; 10680893}. Nuclear pleomorphism and bizarre giant cells are absent, and necrosis is rarely found {10496598; 10716152; 10680893}. Metaplastic bone formation is present in approximately 50% of tumours, most often in the form of a peripheral shell of woven bone. Aneurysmal bone cyst&ndash;like changes may be seen. Vascular invasion is identified in about 30% of tumours {10496598; 10680893}. Additional histological features include stromal haemorrhage (50%) and regressive changes in the form of marked stromal fibrosis and clusters of foamy macrophages (70%). Immunohistochemistry is not helpful.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T16:51:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 406,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 239,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58757,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 56,
        "headingId": 239,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:47:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 407,
